---
title: "Principles of Baking"
code: "BAK-128"
category: "baking-and-pastry-arts"
credits: "3"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
---

Instructs the student in the preparation of breads, pastries, baked desserts, candies, frozen confections, and sugar work. Applies scientific principles and techniques of baking. Promotes the knowledge/skills required to prepare baked items, pastries and confections. Lecture 2 hours. Laboratory 3 hours. Total 5 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
